WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.089 --> 00:00:07.999
Yes, because there was a chapel there.

00:00:07.999 --> 00:00:13.160
And for whatever reason, the chapel captivated
us.

00:00:13.160 --> 00:00:17.029
I think because the building, if I remember,
was round.

00:00:17.029 --> 00:00:23.610
There were no statues which, coming from St.
Mary's in Cambridge, you had statues everywhere.

00:00:23.610 --> 00:00:26.300
So it was just kind of an odd place to go.

00:00:26.300 --> 00:00:31.619
We did find out where the cafeteria was, and
sometimes we could go in and get free sandwiches,

00:00:31.619 --> 00:00:35.890
depending on who was working the cafeteria.

00:00:35.890 --> 00:00:39.690
As kids we would wander through these buildings,
and as I walked down the corridor to come

00:00:39.690 --> 00:00:43.510
to this room that's the memory I have of MIT.

00:00:43.510 --> 00:00:48.290
Those buildings with all the concrete walls
and all the pipes in the ceiling, that's how

00:00:48.290 --> 00:00:52.290
I thought of it for many, many years.

00:00:52.290 --> 00:00:54.960
Very strongly built buildings, like a fortress.

00:00:54.960 --> 00:00:56.660
But for us, we were kids.

00:00:56.660 --> 00:00:59.110
MIT was just like some other place.

00:00:59.110 --> 00:01:01.289
We'd find places to play stickball and tag
football.

00:01:01.289 --> 00:01:06.140
As long as you didn't get kicked out by security
that's kind of what you did.

00:01:06.140 --> 00:01:11.109
One time we were actually allowed to go and
they taught us fencing.

00:01:11.109 --> 00:01:17.029
So as young kids we were able to put on the
mask and use the swords and do some fencing

00:01:17.029 --> 00:01:19.829
too, which I thought was great.

00:01:19.829 --> 00:01:23.079
No, I used to like the smells in there.

00:01:23.079 --> 00:01:30.630
The chemicals and you'd go down the hallways
and you'd smell the different chemicals, and

00:01:30.630 --> 00:01:35.389
the other place was the welding.

00:01:35.389 --> 00:01:39.219
They used to make all different objects.

00:01:39.219 --> 00:01:43.499
I used to like to stick my head in there and
see them welding.

00:01:43.499 --> 00:01:45.560
I used to go and look at the ships.

00:01:45.560 --> 00:01:50.389
They had some model ships when you went through
one of the side doors, and we'd always go

00:01:50.389 --> 00:01:53.270
and look at the model ships.

00:01:53.270 --> 00:01:59.079
I don't know if they were built by people
from MIT, but we'd look at the ships.

00:01:59.079 --> 00:02:07.049
And oh, just walking up those steps and turning
around and looking back across the campus.

00:02:07.049 --> 00:02:08.189
You felt important.

